  "metric_name": "FDC-behavior (Fitness-Distance Correlation in behavior space)",
  "definition": "Sample genes uniformly in bounds; honest-evaluate each (avg over honest_n_trials); estimate global-best behavior b* = behavior of the max-fitness sampled gene; for each sample compute proximity = -||behavior - b*||; FDC = Pearson corr(fitness, proximity); deceptiveness = 1 - max(0, FDC). Easy/non-deceptive -> FDC~+1 -> deceptiveness~0; deceptive -> FDC low/negative -> deceptiveness>=1. Applies to any (genotype,behavior,fitness) landscape.",
